From cf2337b989734735126a953c8e031a9a85748c56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Kostersitz <mkostersitz@mac.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 16:58:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] DuoPanelGeometry: one source of truth for the Surface Duo
 panels and hinge

Pure-Java helper that returns the two panel rects and the hinge band for the
current display size and rotation (spanned, gapless, single panel), so system UI,
Launcher3 and the window manager can stop using literals such as 1344 or 2500.
Same geometry table as the DisplayMask HingeMath (Duo 1350/84/1800, Duo 2
1344/66/1892). No runtime user yet; this is the base for keeping UI off the
hinge. Host unit tests: DuoPanelGeometryTests (11 cases, all rotations).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: Idd71e67a9646c6f816812980c112e6f99dd7d1d8
---
